  "description": "Per-account accumulation, then one break carrying the SUM. Account 1 has two categories - 1000.00 at fifteen percent, which is exactly 12.50, and 2000.00 at twenty-five percent, whose 41.6666... truncates to 41.66 - and ADD WS-MONTHLY-INT TO WS-TOTAL-INT at :467 accumulates them to 54.16. The third record belongs to account 2, so TRANCAT-ACCT-ID differs from WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM at :194, WS-FIRST-TIME is no longer 'Y', and 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT rewrites ACCOUNT 1 - the record still in WORKING-STORAGE - BEFORE :203 reads account 2. Its balance goes from 194.00 to 248.16. Account 2 is the last group and is never rewritten. Note what the sum is not: 54.17, which is what accumulating rounded values would give, and 54.16666..., which is what accumulating exactly and truncating once at the end would give. The COBOL truncates each monthly figure before it accumulates, and the difference is a cent.",
